A||||7||loafer87gt||Slow turbo V6 times||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||10-11-2000||04:15 PM||||I was just reading through this months issue of Kit Car and a guy has built up a 308 replica. What I found interesting is that he has had a performance rebuild on his 2.8, and is using 1.6 ration RR and a more agressive cam, 21 pnd per hour injectors, different pistons, and a millier woods turbo running 14 pounds of boost. Sounds neat huh, well he's only running 14.7 in the quarter mile!! Doesn't this seem very slow to you guys, I think I read in one of 1FAST2M6's post that his GT was running 14's just with tuning and the 4 speed tranny. Or is this about right for a modded v6?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||10-11-2000||05:40 PM||||Just out of curiosity Loafer what was the curb weight with the Kit on it?<P>It does seem kinda of slow if it hada performance cam on it. If not and it was stock engine with the turbo I would say no it seems very good. But with other mods hmm<P>I would think it would be a little faster <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/501b4920.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||10-11-2000||06:44 PM||||Sounds like his injectors are too small.I have 40lb/hr in my 3.8 Buick GN.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||10-11-2000||09:33 PM||||I read the same article and I was shocked.  He said that he was running 14lbs of boost!  So what the hell is his problem?  Too heavy, excessive wheelspin, or maybe he just can't drive worth crap...  I'm hoping for 14.3's or so with my 3.2 project.  1fst was able to pull a 14.7 N/A so I think it's possible.  The only difference will be more displacement and a different clutch.  I'll still be running a new ACT clutch that is slightly less aggressive.  By the time the track re-opens, I should also have new wheels with some wider tires as well.  Winter sucks...  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-12-2000||10:27 AM||||yeah.. GT Bastards car will pull 14.7. with factory ported manifolds and tuning. (probly still close to that with a BAD bearing!) there is something WAY wrong with that turbo set up... improper fueling, timing, not boost retard or somthing... does it say if he has a Haltech e6 or MSD BTM? or any boost provisions? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||10-13-2000||08:03 AM||||I have seen an otherwise stock turbo'd 2.8 running 14.4's with under 10lb of boost. Something is not right in the car you are talking about.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||10-13-2000||10:15 AM||||We don't know if the guy is running a FMU for fuel management or not, so the 21lb inj could be enough for him.  I've seen some wackey things, like people with 19lb injectors running 11's with an FMU, and I've seen 36lb inj without a FMU put up 550 rwhp.  It all depends on the tune.<P>This looks like a classic case of all the right parts, but none of them working together.  What kind of MPH was he putting up?  Thats a better indication of the tune than ET, which is heavily driver influenced.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
